// PLAYTEST: a Saboteur's affliction is a stun. Is a round taken off the
// pack worth a round taken off you?
//
// One of seven files — `player-class-striker`, `-bastion`, `-medic`,
// `-saboteur`, `-leech`, `-invoker`, `-decompiler` — identical in every field but `character`. See
// `player-class-striker.ron` for the shared argument: why the pack is this
// pack, why the pool is unspent, and why **the headless bin reports the same
// numbers for all seven** (it plays All-Attack and invokes nothing, so it is
// the floor rather than the measurement).
//
//     FERAL_DEV_ARENA=1 cargo run  ->  [R] Arena  ->  [L] player-class-saboteur
//
// The floor, 2026-09-01, 20 reps, seeds 1-20: 60% won, mean 18.6 rounds,
// 26% player Integrity left, 1.15 companions down. Compare deltas within one
// build only.
//
// **A stun is the one starter whose worth does not scale with affinity the
// way the other four do.** Hard Lock Single is `Debuff(kind: Stun, power: 0,
// duration: 2)` — the affinity multiplier acts on `power`, which is zero
// here, so a Saboteur's 1.3 may be buying nothing at all on this particular
// routine while the Striker's 1.3 buys 30% more damage. If that is what you
// see, it is a *content* finding about the shipped starter pool, not a
// tuning one: the fix is a starter whose debuff carries a magnitude, not a
// change to the class.
//
// The 2-turn stun is also the enemy-policy feature that shipped in 0.5.19
// and has been played almost not at all — see
// `docs/measurements/2026-08-10-stun-move-levers.md` for what the tuner
// found and could not find.
//
// What to watch:
//   - Whether the affinity moves anything at all. Read the row on the
//     wizard's Routine step as a Saboteur and again as a Medic: if the two
//     print the same numbers, that is the answer before you fight.
//   - Two groups, so there are two front members to lock. Does stunning the
//     front of the *back* group do anything you can see?
//   - Saboteur damps Heal at 0.8, and this kit has no heal, so the trade is
//     invisible here by construction.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 5, zone: 1),
    character: (
        class: Some(Saboteur),
        stats: (0, 0, 0, 0),
        routine: Some("hard_lock"),
    ),
    party: [
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
    ],
    opponents: [
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
    ],
    reps: 1,
    seed: 2,
)
